{"ts": 1784343343.7208166, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the entire episode. Price moved favorably almost immediately after entry and built to a +60.5pt peak around t=5-6m, then gave back a substantial chunk into the +14 to +40pt range through t=16m, but never once crossed back to negative territory. The pullback looked like normal profit-taking/chop within a strong favorable move (giveback stats were against small recent sub-legs, not the whole trade), not a wrong-direction reversal, so thesis stayed intact throughout and I never saw a bail signal. Next time I'd watch for the price actually crossing back toward/through zero (not just local-leg giveback%) as the real wrong-direction tell, since local giveback climbed as high as 145% on a tiny leg while the trade was still deeply profitable overall.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 17}
